{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers","id":1529608,"title":"J.F. Sambrano's Glass Walkers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-28T15:55:15-08:00","id":1529608,"title":"J.F. Sambrano's Glass Walkers","content":"From James' Patreon, another look at what may have been if Hunter's continued with their work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Glass Walkers</b><br /> J.F. Sambrano<br /> <br /> <b>Who are the Glass Walkers</b><br /> The most progressive Tribe, the Glass Walkers are branded Urrah by other Garou, who believe them to be chained to the Weaver's webs. The Glass Walkers, however, feel that the Weaver is suffering, twisted from her original purpose much as the Wyrm is, and deserves to be guided in a direction that will encourage her to reclaim her true role--the Protector. Glass Walkers are innovative, economical, and willing to buck the traditionalist attitude of hardliners and and those incapable of adapting. More than any other Tribe, the Glass Walkers are open to young Garou who look back on the mistakes of the past with trepidation and horror, and invite them to their future-first perspective.<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers favor efficiency, made up of technicians, scientists, and logicians, and prefer to approach the unsolved equation of the Malady from that angle. They choose to live in the Scabs, which most Garou avoid like they would the realms of the Wyrm itself, combating the corruption from within the belly of the spider. The Glass Walkers concern themselves with green sciences and technologies, which undeniably promote the goals of the Garou. If nothing else, the Glass Walkers are adaptable, and almost never find themselves out of place in changing times--save with their own cousins.<br /> <br /> <b>Gaia's Howl</b><br /> Every problem has a solution, and Gaia's Howl is not different. If a solution does not immediately present itself, then a workaround must be invented, or the Garou must innovate an entirely new approach--the sundering of the Umbra from the material world poses many problems, but they are within the grasp of the Glass Walkers to resolve.<br /> <br /> A new philosophy, dedicated to the concept of the Intelligent Machine, has spread like wildfire throughout the Tribe. The proponents of the Machine believe that through innovative and creative technology combined with the power of spirits of the Weaver's Court, they can bring the physical world and the Umbra together once again--something they see as necessary in order to accomplish their primary function, preserving and protecting Gaia herself.<br /> <br /> Most Glass Walkers hold to a controversial belief, which they feel must be addressed if the Garou are going have any success relieving Gaia's suffering, and they refuse to walk on eggshells about it anymore. The Wyld is also out of balance, and is just as dangerous as the Weaver and the Wyrm. They purport that the Wyld has always acted out of chaos and madness, and it is this turmoil that forced the other parts of the Triat to over-correct. To them, this is clearly evidenced by humanity being increasingly under threat by natural disasters such as earthquakes, floods, and dangerous hurricanes, even if such things can be tied to the human destruction of the natural world. Like the rest of the Apocalyptic signs, they answer is logical and critical thinking applied through technological and spiritual transformation.<br /> <br /> <b>The Malady</b><br /> The Glass Walkers are a Tribe of survivors and have always used adoption as a primary method of bolstering their numbers. They argue that no other Tribe is more cognizant of useful technologies such as facial recognition and GPS tracking which, spiritually awakened, can be directly applied to seeking out Lost Cubs. What they don't discuss is that their techniques hardly make them gifted at tracking down their wolf-born kin, and that the Malady has all but cemented this Tribe as completely losing its bestial ties.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers tend to take in any kin who are open-minded, unafraid of change, and in particular favor the analytical and inventive. More than any of these traits, a Glass Walker must show a penchant for adaptability in order to earn the favor of the Cockroach.<br /> <br /> Corruption and apocalyptic disaster are the result of both the dangers of nature and the willingness of humanity to use their gifts of intelligence and tool-making to further their own ideas of need and greed, rather than inventing a new world capable of protecting all. The Glass Walkers are set to uncover a solution, whether it require code and creation, or claws and a rain of lead.<br /> <br /> <b>Archetypes</b><br /> Inventors, scientists, lawyers, hostile takeover specialists, Machine cultists.<br /> <br /> <b>Kinfolk</b><br /> The Glass Walkers would say that they have always treated their Kinfolk well and with respect. Centuries ago, they called themselves the Warders of Men and to this day they take that role seriously and the humans which they treat with the most are their own families. Glass Walkers also heavily believe in adoptive families, inviting people to their table who act as siblings or cousins.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they have never treated their wolf Kinfolk well, what few even exist. At best, the wolf relatives of the Glass Walkers might be kept as exotic pets in penthouse apartments, or behind the safety of walls and fences in wolf sanctuaries. At worst the Glass Walkers experiment on their wolf Kinfolk with genetic manipulation and other methods in order to make them hardier, healthier, and more fertile.<br /> <br /> <b>Cockroach</b><br /> The Patron Spirit of the Glass Walkers is Cockroach, who often earns an immediate response of revulsion due to his association with uncleanliness and decay. However, the reality is that cockroach is a survivor, adapting to any environment he is set to. Whether making his home deep in the wild of the jungles, or within the disharmony of urban decay, cockroach always endures. Cockroach teaches his children that they cannot balk at making the choices that will help them survive, and is a spirit of Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <b>Harmony</b><br /> Despite the argument that some Garou make that the Glass Walkers are lost to the Weaver, and dangerously unbalanced in that way, the Glass Walkers themselves are one of a few tribes who truly sees that the cycle exists that way for a reason, and try to run themselves through that cycle in their own lives. They find Harmony through using the destructive and reductive energies of the Wyrm to aid the Wyld through concepts such as composting, or recycling. They assist the Great Spider with the tools of the Wyld by engaging in urban permaculture or genetically modified organisms.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghreena</b><br /> The Ghreena of the Glass Walkers is the sterilization of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers flip the usual narrative of the Triat represented by Garou on its head, suggesting that the Wyld is at fault for driving the Weaver mad, which resulted in its machinations on the Wyrm. They will turn the tools of the Weaver on the Wyld with intent, building dams that provide &quot;clean energy&quot; while destroying ecosystems, genetically modifying crops to make them more durable against weather and pests, or creating low carbon footprint technologies which require mining operations that poison animals, people, and waterways. Many Glass Walkers favor terraforming the &quot;undesirable&quot; aspects of Gaia, such as deserts, by diverting waterways and creating solar panel fields which make these spaces more hospitable for humanity. They might claim that these actions are made out of a need for progress, but they seek out the sterilization of unstable qualities in the environment. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T16:36:23-08:00","id":1529609,"title":"","content":"fascinating!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T16:41:12-08:00","id":1529610,"title":"","content":"Once again, it's really nice to see these tribes rewritten by someone who actually understands the game.<br /> <br /> What stands out to me the most about this particular rewrite is I think it highlights very well why Ghreena is so much smarter of a concept than Hauglosk. This isn't just some blanket statement of &quot;Garou and their methods are Bad&quot;, nor is it ignoring the realities present in the game and what it's always been willing to discuss. The Glass Walker Ghreena here is something that environmental activists have always had to contend with, that some methods of making things cleaner have many of their own problems that need to be addressed to make them not cause plenty of their own harm, and it's realistic that a Glass Walker in the throes of desperation and zealotry would lose sight of keeping things balanced and stop caring. It's working with the game on its own terms, not throwing it in the trash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:02:55-08:00","id":1529611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529610#post1529610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, it's really nice to see these tribes rewritten by someone who actually understands the game.<br /> <br /> What stands out to me the most about this particular rewrite is I think it highlights very well why Ghreena is so much smarter of a concept than Hauglosk. This isn't just some blanket statement of &quot;Garou and their methods are Bad&quot;, nor is it ignoring the realities present in the game and what it's always been willing to discuss. The Glass Walker Ghreena here is something that environmental activists have always had to contend with, that some methods of making things cleaner have many of their own problems that need to be addressed to make them not cause plenty of their own harm, and it's realistic that a Glass Walker in the throes of desperation and zealotry would lose sight of keeping things balanced and stop caring. It's working with the game on its own terms, not throwing it in the trash.</div> </div> </div> </div>honest question,why do you hate werewolf5 so much? it almost feels like it's personal to you,like w5 is a insult to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:03:47-08:00","id":1529612,"title":"","content":"i'm asking cause there's lots of tv shows,comic books,video games whose product i don't like at,but i don't feel their existence is a personal slight to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:09:34-08:00","id":1529613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529611#post1529611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> honest question,why do you hate werewolf5 so much? it almost feels like it's personal to you,like w5 is a insult to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is well-worn ground by this point, so I don't feel a lot like repeating myself. You can read pretty much any of the other threads here about W5 to see the many, many things people have torn apart about it.<br /> <br /> But the short answer is, I treat W5 like an insult because honestly? It kind of <i>is</i>. It was made by lead developers who at best don't care about Werewolf and at worst actively dislike it, and made a lot of the mechanics and flavor to deliberately undermine and insult legacy editions rather than just rebooting it like the game pretends to do. Developers working under the project (especially James Sambrano!) were treated terribly, and the current lead dev decided to not care about anything other than really wanting everyone to know that all Nordic people are Nazis, to the exclusion of actually making a good or coherent game.<br /> <br /> I also don't usually have this much vitriol for things I merely dislike, but W5 is especially offensive as a longtime Werewolf fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:20:46-08:00","id":1529614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529613#post1529613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this is well-worn ground by this point, so I don't feel a lot like repeating myself. You can read pretty much any of the other threads here about W5 to see the many, many things people have torn apart about it.<br /> <br /> But the short answer is, I treat W5 like an insult because honestly? It kind of <i>is</i>. It was made by lead developers who at best don't care about Werewolf and at worst actively dislike it, and made a lot of the mechanics and flavor to deliberately undermine and insult legacy editions rather than just rebooting it like the game pretends to do. Developers working under the project (especially James Sambrano!) were treated terribly, and the current lead dev decided to not care about anything other than really wanting everyone to know that all Nordic people are Nazis, to the exclusion of actually making a good or coherent game.<br /> <br /> I also don't usually have this much vitriol for things I merely dislike, but W5 is especially offensive as a longtime Werewolf fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's funny,maybe it's because i discovered the game very late,but there was so much of it felt needed a update.<br /> Like,let's take the litany as a example.<br /> The Litany tells the garou to <i>kill themselves if they get too old to fight,</i>, the litany tells <i>garouborn are lesser and should be treated with scorn,</i>the litany tells the garou to <i>submit to others if they're stronger than you</i><br /> Honestly,it took me a long time to realize that garou nation was not <i>meant </i>to be well... evil.<br /> w5 turned that evil nation into nothing,or at very least a fraction of itself and I'm happy for it<br /> my player character can build something that <i>actually helps people </i>in its place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 01-28-2024, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:26:26-08:00","id":1529615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529614#post1529614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it's funny,maybe it's because i discovered the game very late,but there was so much of it felt needed a update.<br /> Like,let's take the litany as a example.<br /> The Litany tells the garou to <i>kill themselves if they get too old to fight,</i>, the litany tells <i>garouborn are lesser and should be treated with scorn,</i>the litany tells the garou to <i>submit to others if they're stronger than you</i><br /> Honestly,it took me a long time to realize that garou nation was not <i>meant </i>to be well... evil.<br /> w5 turned that evil nation into nothing,or at very least a fraction of itself and I'm happy for it<br /> my player character can build something that <i>actually helps people </i>in its place.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise that with that (and every other) law comes a whole bevy of interpretation? That there are three whole auspices tasked with recording, understanding, challenging and interpreting what those laws mean?<br /> <br /> Both in the old corebooks and the tribebooks there's quite a bit of text on what the laws mean in spirit and what they mean in practice. And that for most tribes it's not &quot;kill yourself if you're old or unhealthy&quot;. There is no context or interpretation on the Litany in W5 to discuss any of that, though. But since the Litany is for losers and completely irrelevant in W5...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:40:36-08:00","id":1529616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529614#post1529614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it's funny,maybe it's because i discovered the game very late,but there was so much of it felt needed a update.<br /> Like,let's take the litany as a example.<br /> The Litany tells the garou to <i>kill themselves if they get too old to fight,</i>,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unless they're getting slow, doddering, or otherwise excessively holding back the pack; most of the time, if they're getting slower or weaker, they'll die in battle, anyway. And nowadays, this tenet could be used against bad leaders with almost surgical precision.<br /> <br /> (Also worth noting that in Forsaken, the Firstborn did exactly this to Father/Mother Wolf, if you want to contrast things.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the litany tells <i>garouborn are lesser and should be treated with scorn,</i> </div> </div> </div><i><br /> <br /> Respect Those Beneath Ye, All Are Of Gaia. The Litany has this one simple trick - Shadow Lords hate it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> </div> </div> </div></i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the litany tells the garou to <i>submit to others if they're stronger than you</i> </div> </div> </div>Higher in Rank. They are technically a military organization, it's kind of to be expected, even if not entirely laudable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly,it took me a long time to realize that garou nation was not <i>meant </i>to be well... evil. </div> </div> </div>It's meant to be extremely difficult to work with if you're trying to make a difference, as it is a system that's been ensconced in a war for a long time and has been pushed from a position of being an official, powerful organization in the world to a guerilla organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> w5 turned that evil nation into nothing,or at very least a fraction of itself and I'm happy for it<br /> my player character can build something that <i>actually helps people </i>in its place. </div> </div> </div>W5 can't really be said to have done anything. It's all over the place. It also evaded the question of the Crinos-born by ignoring that they existed, and pushes the Lupus into much the same position as a detail that it doesn't want to deal with. It's trying to dodge rather than address and own problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:42:47-08:00","id":1529617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529615#post1529615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realise that with that (and every other) law comes a whole bevy of interpretation? That there are three whole auspices tasked with recording, understanding, challenging and interpreting what those laws mean?<br /> <br /> Both in the old corebooks and the tribebooks there's quite a bit of text on what the laws mean in spirit and what they mean in practice. And that for most tribes it's not &quot;kill yourself if you're old or unhealthy&quot;. There is no context or interpretation on the Litany in W5 to discuss any of that, though. But since the Litany is for losers and completely irrelevant in W5...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to see your point Asmodai, mostly because you seem like a genuinely nice person, but given their bloody history,numerous (and i mean <i>numerous) </i>morally abhorrent acts, the litany as a whole and their overall cultish behaviour its really hard for me to see a Garou Nation that could achieve its goals,honestly &quot;The Garou Nation <i>needs </i> to fall&quot; is a bit of a party line for me. They failed so much,they hurt so many people,every step forwards for them was followed by about a billion steps back.<br /> that's why i like the tribs of w5, they're <i>fresh,new free of past baggage and mistakes of the past.</i>They can actually <i>do </i>something to help the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 01-28-2024, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:44:49-08:00","id":1529618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529617#post1529617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm trying to see your point Asmoday,mostly because you seem like a genuinely nice person, but given their bloody history,numerous (and i mean <i>numerous) </i>morally abhorrent acts, the litany as a whole and their overall cultish behaviour its really hard for me to see a Garou Nation that could achieve its goals,honestly &quot;The Garou Nation <i>needs </i> to fall&quot; is a bit of a party line for me. They failed so much,they hurt so many people,every step forwards for them was followed by about a billion steps back.<br /> that's why i like the tribs of w5, they're <i>fresh,new free of past baggage and mistakes of the past.</i>They can actually <i>do </i>something to help the world</div> </div> </div> </div>lemme challenge you, there are 44 example wolfs in w5. 4 archetypes for each tribe, how many of them are helping people? or the world,in any way shape or form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:49:46-08:00","id":1529619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529617#post1529617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm trying to see your point Asmoday,mostly because you seem like a genuinely nice person, but given their bloody history,numerous (and i mean <i>numerous) </i>morally abhorrent acts, the litany as a whole and their overall cultish behaviour its really hard for me to see a Garou Nation that could achieve its goals,honestly &quot;The Garou Nation <i>needs </i> to fall&quot; is a bit of a party line for me. They failed so much,they hurt so many people,every step forwards for them was followed by about a billion steps back.<br /> that's why i like the tribs of w5, they're <i>fresh,new free of past baggage and mistakes of the past.</i>They can actually <i>do </i>something to help the world</div> </div> </div> </div>The Red Talons are now actively cannibalistic (something this &quot;toxic, outdated, cultish&quot; litany previously condemned) and one of their example characters spreads diseases to human villages for funsies, and another locks people up in the prison industrial complex, again, seemingly for funsies. The Black Furies are accelerationist social darwinists and just aimlessly lash out at things by the admission of their own writeup. Most of the other Tribes are just kind of sitting around doing nothing, and there's a sidebar that says that corporations are Good Community Actions, while the Garou's direct action is Bad Community Action.<br /> <br /> I fail to see how any of this is an improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 01-28-2024, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:52:39-08:00","id":1529620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529618#post1529618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> lemme challenge you, there are 44 example wolfs in w5. 4 archetypes for each tribe, how many of them are helping people? or the world,in any way shape or form.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black Fury EMT probably saved quite a few's people lives,Same for the Glass Walker Detective","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T17:58:27-08:00","id":1529621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529620#post1529620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Black Fury EMT probably saved quite a few's people lives,Same for the Glass Walker Detective</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Probably.&quot;<br /> <br /> These are things that any human could do though. The only ones doing any good are doing it in a very mundane, small-scale human way. Why even bother playing a werewolf? Especially when a lot of the other example characters are uh. &quot;Protecting the private land of the landed gentry,&quot; &quot;spreading diseases&quot;, &quot;working for the prison-industrial complex&quot;, &quot;dealing drugs&quot;, &quot;stealing cars for no reason&quot;, &quot;right-wing doomsday prepper&quot;, and other lovely things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 01-28-2024, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T18:19:28-08:00","id":1529622,"title":"","content":"ok guys,i'll do something i really don't like to do.<br /> I admit i was wrong.<br /> This is a pattern with me,i get angry,i start arguing with people until my own arguments don't make no sense to me and i have to admit I'm wrong.<br /> This time i realized i was wrong when Fox and Saurs reminded me the Litany has <i>11 </i>laws.<br /> I only focused on 3,and i based my whole argument on how the evil the garou nation was on it.<br /> for that I'm sorry,my only excuse is that the three laws i latched on as basis for my baseless hatred are based on 3 bad experiences I've been through<br /> &quot;Garou Shall Not Mate With Garou &quot;(the anti garouborn law) reminded me past times where i suffered ableism<br /> &quot;Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness&quot; reminded of elder abuse and i spent a long time taking care of my sick grandma before she passed in 2020<br /> &quot;Submit to Those of Higher Station&quot; i was really dumb with this one,i thought it meant &quot;submit to those who have bigger muscles or fight better or are just taller&quot; (I'm 5'6 and get shit for it)<br /> i know that those 3 laws reminding me of bad times i've had is not a excuse for just saying the Garou Nation needeed to fall, specially as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> cleverly demonstrated, a lot of garou interpreted the litany their own way.<br /> I'm sorry. i get overly defensive of w5 because i waited for it for 3 years,and i was SO happy when i got my pdf and my book. And sometimes i feel like certain comments are taking my happiness away from me, it's not fair for me to accuse people,fictiional or real of crimes just because of my own bad experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T18:27:48-08:00","id":1529623,"title":"","content":"So... going back to the write up of the Glass Walkers that aren't:<br /> <br /> While I like a lot of the approach, I really wish there was some contrast to the Bone Gnawers; as fellow Scab inhabiting adapt-and-survive focused Garou. There's justifiably a lot of how different the GWs are from the rest of the Nation, but it would be nice to see a sentence or two about the Tribe they're most compared to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T18:29:12-08:00","id":1529624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529622#post1529622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok guys,i'll do something i really don't like to do.<br /> I admit i was wrong.<br /> This is a pattern with me,i get angry,i start arguing with people until my own arguments don't make no sense to me and i have to admit I'm wrong.<br /> This time i realized i was wrong when Fox and Saurs reminded me the Litany has <i>11 </i>laws.<br /> I only focused on 3,and i based my whole argument on how the evil the garou nation was on it.<br /> for that I'm sorry,my only excuse is that the three laws i latched on as basis for my baseless hatred are based on 3 bad experiences I've been through<br /> &quot;Garou Shall Not Mate With Garou &quot;(the anti garouborn law) reminded me past times where i suffered ableism<br /> &quot;Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness&quot; reminded of elder abuse and i spent a long time taking care of my sick grandma before she passed in 2020<br /> &quot;Submit to Those of Higher Station&quot; i was really dumb with this one,i thought it meant &quot;submit to those who have bigger muscles or fight better or are just taller&quot; (I'm 5'6 and get shit for it)<br /> i know that those 3 laws reminding me of bad times i've had is not a excuse for just saying the Garou Nation needeed to fall, specially as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> cleverly demonstrated, a lot of garou interpreted the litany their own way.<br /> I'm sorry. i get overly defensive of w5 because i waited for it for 3 years,and i was SO happy when i got my pdf and my book. And sometimes i feel like certain comments are taking my happiness away from me, it's not fair for me to accuse people,fictiional or real of crimes just because of my own bad experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, it's okay. I totally get it. Sometimes things just react with you in a particular way due to personal experience, and you have to step back and take them in context, or know when to step away for your own mental health.<br /> <br /> And trust me, no one is happy that W5 turned out this way. I would have loved a properly-updated and simplified version of WtA for newcomers to get into, and to clean up things from older editions that were outdated. It's just a shame the lead devs apparently didn't agree with this sentiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T18:31:16-08:00","id":1529625,"title":"","content":"thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T18:59:31-08:00","id":1529626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529623#post1529623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... going back to the write up of the Glass Walkers that aren't:<br /> <br /> While I like a lot of the approach, I really wish there was some contrast to the Bone Gnawers; as fellow Scab inhabiting adapt-and-survive focused Garou. There's justifiably a lot of how different the GWs are from the rest of the Nation, but it would be nice to see a sentence or two about the Tribe they're most compared to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda feel like the big contrast from older editions that's also on display here, other than the obvious &quot;upper-class vs lower-class&quot;, is their approach towards the Weaver. The Bone Gnawers don't have any particular attachment towards the Weaver, and the only reason they're in the cities is because that's where the downtrodden are these days, and it's territory no one else is willing to protect. They're just as likely to settle in run-down rural areas if that's where their fight takes them. The Glass Walkers actively immerse themselves in the Weaver's tools and domains and here the connection is made even more explicit by them, at their most extreme, turning on the Wyld to help the Weaver, something the Bone Gnawers definitely wouldn't do.<br /> <br /> That said, it would probably be easier to see that contrast if we had the Bone Gnawer writeup to compare it to, which would have been the context this was initially meant to be read in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T19:01:35-08:00","id":1529627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529623#post1529623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... going back to the write up of the Glass Walkers that aren't:<br /> <br /> While I like a lot of the approach, I really wish there was some contrast to the Bone Gnawers; as fellow Scab inhabiting adapt-and-survive focused Garou. There's justifiably a lot of how different the GWs are from the rest of the Nation, but it would be nice to see a sentence or two about the Tribe they're most compared to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that a Gnawer writeup would involve way less use of theoretical cosmological principles to explain why they're doing what they're doing and living where they are. Because, after all, there are a lot of rural Bone Gnawers who might not be quite as at home in the city as all Glass Walkers would be, and who aren't there to try their hand at being a City Farmer or Urban Primitive. The Gnawers have also, at least since Revised, had the division in their patron as being about nurturing care and bloody vengeance in Mother Rat vs. The Rat God, which is a marked difference from the unified front of Cockroach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T20:00:42-08:00","id":1529629,"title":"","content":"OK, but that's all coming from legacy perspectives. There are some serious, if subtle shifts in the Glass Walkers in this take on them.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I'm not saying take a huge amount of space on it, but a little. Especially since not everyone reads each Tribe write up. A player might check out one Tribe because it sounds cool, and not read up on the lines between similar Tribes as they start thinking up ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T01:28:23-08:00","id":1529633,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure who the writer was for the Bone Gnawer writeup in the HE version.....I'd honestly love to see all the writeups but I know a few of the writers still have tangential bridges with Paradox that they might not want to burn by releasing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T02:44:51-08:00","id":1529635,"title":"","content":"I freaking love the <b>Ghreena</b> of the GWs. One of the things that has always bothered me with the Walkers is how their negatives are rarely ever discussed. This showcases exactly why other garou might see them as tainted and yet it makes perfect sense for a tribe of Progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T08:36:22-08:00","id":1529644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529629#post1529629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but that's all coming from legacy perspectives. There are some serious, if subtle shifts in the Glass Walkers in this take on them.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I'm not saying take a huge amount of space on it, but a little. Especially since not everyone reads each Tribe write up. A player might check out one Tribe because it sounds cool, and not read up on the lines between similar Tribes as they start thinking up ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, agreed. This comes from a rough draft and before the other tribes were finalised, so I assume someone would have added something when they knew how the other side of the City coin would operate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T08:40:50-08:00","id":1529645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529622#post1529622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry. i get overly defensive of w5 because i waited for it for 3 years,and i was SO happy when i got my pdf and my book. And sometimes i feel like certain comments are taking my happiness away from me, it's not fair for me to accuse people,fictiional or real of crimes just because of my own bad experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me, all of us were waiting for a new, better version of Werewolf and have put money towards it. Seeing this as a result was a deep disappointment for us, especially as we were keenly aware of certain issues with the game. But our passion comes from what the game could be and the great ideas that it introduced, and how much it worked on its own legacy to improve the errors of its ways. It's incredibly saddening to see something near and dear to you be turned upside down and inside out by someone missing the point of what you cared for.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry you felt bad about it, but you don't have to like something just because you wasted money, passion and expectations on it. You get to choose what you enjoy, and if you find something in W5 that makes you sing, then stick to it and be happy with it. Just don't feel that you have to fight for something that you aren't happy with.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T09:49:44-08:00","id":1529651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529608-j-f-sambrano-s-glass-walkers?p=1529645#post1529645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trust me, all of us were waiting for a new, better version of Werewolf and have put money towards it. Seeing this as a result was a deep disappointment for us, especially as we were keenly aware of certain issues with the game. But our passion comes from what the game could be and the great ideas that it introduced, and how much it worked on its own legacy to improve the errors of its ways. It's incredibly saddening to see something near and dear to you be turned upside down and inside out by someone missing the point of what you cared for.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry you felt bad about it, but you don't have to like something just because you wasted money, passion and expectations on it. You get to choose what you enjoy, and if you find something in W5 that makes you sing, then stick to it and be happy with it. Just don't feel that you have to fight for something that you aren't happy with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I did enjoy reading w5 and being the storyteller's of a game before i got too busy to continue. It Doesn't make it automatically good obviously,but it certainly brought me lots of fun times alone and helped make me friends, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T05:48:24-08:00","id":1529701,"title":"","content":"I have to say that this take really nails the Glass Walkers - their attitude is perfectly rational but other bits of it just make me growl (I\u2019m an Old Country Garou at heart).<br /> <br /> One has to admit that I\u2019m always happy to see Cockroach at the heart of the Walkers: it\u2019s a nice reminder that they\u2019re not all Random Interrupts all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}